# Gate step — data, not code (order 1072-b7eq). Moved from an inline build.sh
# --check block by the .step series (2253-j2at batch 2): as a .step it is no
# build.sh edit, so it never makes intake HEAVY, and it runs in the pool (a
# read-only decider: it reads the tree and the diff, writes nothing).
#
# Order 941-trcf. The fragment-overlay cost is linear in the index.d
# backlog (~40ms of gate time per fragment per gate run, measured), so the
# gate NAMES the backlog before it regrows to the 338 that doubled it.
# ADVISORY on the 751-i9mb terms: a grown backlog is news for the next
# coordination cycle, never a build break.
STEP_DESC="Checking the plan fragment backlog against the compaction cadence (941-trcf, advisory)"
STEP_LUA="scripts/lua/check-fragment-backlog.lua"
STEP_ERROR="the fragment-backlog advisory could not run — that is a broken checkout, not a clean backlog"
STEP_OK="Fragment-backlog advisory reported"
STEP_READS="scripts/lua/check-fragment-backlog.lua"
